## 11. Expected Outcomes

The proposed testing methodology will establish a systematic process for validating the AutoLink RadioSense LoRa communication subsystem.

The raw-packet testing phase will establish baseline radio performance and characterize the effects of radio parameters, distance, environmental conditions, and mobility.

The final-packet testing phase will verify the correctness and operational reliability of the application packet structure while quantifying its communication performance under comparable experimental conditions.

The resulting dataset will provide empirical evidence for selecting appropriate radio configurations and evaluating the communication subsystem. These findings can subsequently support the development and evaluation of higher-level AutoLink RadioSense functionality, including link-quality assessment and multi-hop routing.

The testing framework will therefore serve as the foundation for both reliable system implementation and reproducible experimental evaluation of the AutoLink RadioSense project.
